  <title id="bdl15ivonflatminimum-title">Loss landscape with the MAP solution in a sharp minimum and the IVON solution in a flat region</title>
  <desc id="bdl15ivonflatminimum-desc">A shaded map of a two-parameter loss, darker for lower loss, with a colour bar from 0 to 20. The low-loss region is a wedge whose narrow tip lies near the lower left and which widens toward the upper right; outside the wedge the loss rises quickly. The MAP solution, a cross, sits in a small narrow pit near the tip of the wedge. The IVON solution, a dot surrounded by a circle that marks one posterior standard deviation, lies far inside the wide part of the wedge, where the loss stays low over the whole circle.</desc>
